## HackMD MCP (Model Context Protocol)

HackMD hosts an official remote MCP server so AI assistants can read and write notes inside a conversation.

The MCP server authenticates with **OAuth 2.1**. The REST API and CLI continue to use personal API tokens; the two are independent.

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Server URL** | `https://mcp.hackmd.io/` |
| **Transport** | Streamable HTTP |
| **Auth** | OAuth 2.1 (authorization code + PKCE) |
| **Scope** | `mcp` |
| **Resource metadata** | [`/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource`](https://mcp.hackmd.io/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource) (RFC 9728) |
| **Authorization server** | `https://hackmd.io` — see [`/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server`](https://hackmd.io/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server) |

### Connecting

Most MCP clients need only the server URL; the client opens a browser window for you to approve access. No API token is required.

```json
{ "mcpServers": { "hackmd": { "url": "https://mcp.hackmd.io/" } } }
```

Unauthenticated requests — including `tools/list` — return **HTTP 401** with a `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm="mcp"` challenge pointing at the resource metadata above. There is no public tool catalog.

- [HackMD MCP Server Setup](https://hackmd.io/@docs/hackmd-mcp-setup) — per-client configuration, full tool list, troubleshooting
- Alternate entry: [MCP setup (developer portal book)](https://hackmd.io/@docs/mcp-server-setup)

### Legacy: API token authentication

Clients that cannot complete an OAuth flow may still authenticate with `Authorization: Bearer <API_TOKEN>`, typically via the `mcp-remote` bridge. This path is kept for compatibility only; prefer OAuth. See the setup guide for the exact configuration.

### Tools and resources

Tool names use **kebab-case** (e.g. `list-notes`, `get-note`, `create-note`, `search-notes`). Do not guess `snake_case` names.

Representative tools: `list-notes`, `get-note`, `create-note`, `update-note`, `delete-note`, `list-teams`, `get-team`, `search-notes`, `get-history`, `get-me`. Pass the optional `teamPath` parameter to `list-notes` or `create-note` for a team workspace. See the setup guide for the complete list and parameters.

MCP resources (URI scheme `hackmd://`): `hackmd://notes/{noteId}` (markdown), `hackmd://me` (JSON profile), `hackmd://teams/{teamPath}` (JSON team details).

## AI use policy

- AI **search & answer engines** (e.g. ChatGPT Search, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews) **may** crawl publicly published notes and cite them with attribution.
- AI **foundation-model training** is **not permitted**. See [`/robots.txt`](https://hackmd.io/robots.txt) for the per-vendor declarations (`GPTBot`, `Google-Extended`, `ClaudeBot`, `Applebot-Extended`, `CCBot`, `Meta-ExternalAgent`, `Bytespider`, etc. all `Disallow: /`).
- **User-initiated agents** acting on a logged-in user's behalf may use MCP OAuth or that user's API token under the API policy linked above.
- **Private notes** (HTTP 403 to anonymous requests) must not be accessed, transcribed, or retained.

